# One-off audit harness pointed at the deployed site (screenshots, probes).
# Kept out of the repo: it targets a specific URL and writes large PNGs.
.audit/

# Cloud-sync conflict copies. The sync client on this machine writes
# "name 2.ext" beside a file it thinks diverged, and one of those was
# committed by a `git add -A` before anyone noticed. They are never real
# source, and an unreferenced stale copy of a component is worse than
# useless - it is a second version for the next reader to reconcile.
#
# Anchored to the repo root and scoped to source and asset extensions, so a
# genuine name containing " 2" is untouched: assets/source/logos/NCF 2023.webp
# is a real file and must keep working.
* 2.tsx
* 2.ts
* 2.mjs
* 2.js
* 2.json
* 2.css
* 2.png
* 2.webp
* 2.jpg
* 2.svg
